Answer to open questions:

**Phase 9 – Sky, Time, Seasons and Weather**

- **Phase 9 Q13 – The seasons' representative days:** on World → Time → Season choosing a season moves the date to a day that stands for that season at the world's place, keeping the time of day (Q11). Built as proposed (v4.28), open for confirmation: spring = halfway from the first green to full leaf; early summer = halfway from full leaf to summer; summer = the warmest day; autumn = the peak of the autumn colours; late autumn = when most leaves have fallen; winter = the middle of the snow season at the rider's altitude, else the coldest day; places without deciduous trees go by the temperature's year. The jump goes to the nearest such day: in November "summer" is the past July and "winter" the coming January. Answer: (a) the nearest, as built; 

- **Phase 9 Q14 – Calendar: does choosing a day set it or only select it:** on World → Time a calendar sets the world's date (v4.46). Built for now: a click, Enter or the gamepad's South button on a day sets that date at once and stays on the calendar, so the world changes while browsing; the Select button (9J, v4.45) sets the highlighted day and goes back. In most date pickers a click on a day only highlights it and OK confirms, so browsing never changes anything. Answer: (a) keep both as built; 

Add on: Do check if the Map is in a region where there are seasons. E.g. in Tenerife there are not AFAIK.
